delinquency_roster.json: pulled once on 12 Oct 2026 from the public FDIC BankFind API (https://banks.data.fdic.gov/api/financials, one request, filters CERT:(the 16 certs in config/peers.json) AND REPDTE:[20170331 TO 20260630], fields CERT, REPDTE and the 20 fields of peers/delinquency.FIELDS); 608 rows, 16 banks x 38 quarters 2017Q1-2026Q2, the API's meta total matched, no blank values; kept as {YYYYMMDD: [rows]} like roster_2006.json, one row per bank per quarter, only those fields, sorted by CERT. The pull script was a throwaway and is not kept.
These are the API's values, not the filing's: nothing in this fixture or its tests has been tied to KeyBank's RC-N on the FFIEC CDR (V1-ROUND2-SPEC acceptance item 2 is that check, made separately).

14 Oct 2026: LNCONRP (RC-C 6.b, other revolving credit plans) added to roster_2006.json, roster_1992.json and delinquency_roster.json, one request each to https://api.fdic.gov/banks/financials (filters CERT:(the 16 certs) AND REPDTE:[first TO last], fields CERT, REPDTE, LNCONRP); every row matched, the API's meta totals 1,312, 2,155 and 608. It is blank in every quarter before 2001: the FDIC data has no 6.b until 2001Q1. Other consumer's balance is now 6.b + 6.d; the acceptance tests reproduce the 6 Oct build on a copy with 6.b at 0 (conftest.as_earlier_build), since that build divided by 6.d alone. The script was a throwaway and is not kept.
